        {
          "id": "a_fuel_with_no_energy_content_yields_no_refueling_row",
          "description": "REFEC-7 joins each energy row to RefuelingFuelType, whose extract keeps only `energyContent > 0 AND fuelDensity > 0`. Electricity has NULL for both, so the join misses and the row is DROPPED -- which is the whole of why the fixture's spillage block is 208 rows and not 250, even though sourcetypetechadjustment gives every model year a spillage rate. Row 3 pins that zero, and rows 1 and 2 beside it pin the same expression on a fuel that does have a divisor, so the zero is the join missing and not the arithmetic failing.",
